    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0383" n="371" xml:id="pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24591/12–544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-05T14:00:00+03:25">December 5, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>103. During Medjliss debate on new Cabinet,<anchor n="35" xml:id="d376-f1"/> two
                    or three deputies criticized absence of treaty or other legal sanction for
                    presence of American troops in Iran. In his reply yesterday Premier Bay at gave
                    assurance that action would be taken to conclude a special agreement on this
                    subject at earliest possible moment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d376-f1" n="35" xml:id="d376-f1-content">
                <p>A new Iranian Government had been formed November 26 by Morteza Qoli Bayat.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
